questions.solution:
Leaching is a process in which powdered ore is treated with certain reagents, which dissolves the ore leaving behind impurities in undissolved form. Aluminium ore is concentrated by this method, bauxite $\left(\mathrm{Al}_2 \mathrm{O}_3 \cdot 2 \mathrm{H}_2 \mathrm{O}\right)$ contain ferric oxide, titanium oxide and silica as impurities.
Bauxite is treated with aqueous solution of caustic soda. Alumina get dissolved forming soluble sodium aluminate leaving behind impurities.

\mathrm{Al}_2 \mathrm{O}_3+6 \mathrm{NaOH} \longrightarrow 2 \mathrm{Na}_3 \mathrm{AlO}_3+3 \mathrm{H}_2 \mathrm{O}

questions.q:
Arrange the aqueous solutions of the following salts in the increasing order of $\mathrm{pH}$
\begin{array}{ccc}
\mathrm{CuSO}_4 & \mathrm{NaCN} & \mathrm{KCl} \\
\mathrm{I} & \text { II } & \text { III }
\end{array}

questions.solution:
$\mathrm{NaCN}$ is the salt of strong base $(\mathrm{NaOH})$ and weak acid (HCN). So, its $\mathrm{pH} \gt 7$.
$\mathrm{CuSO}_4$ is a salt of strong acid $\left(\mathrm{H}_2 \mathrm{SO}_4\right)$ and a weak base $\left[\mathrm{Cu}(\mathrm{OH})_2\right.$, thus its solution is acidic with $\mathrm{pH} \lt  7$.
$\mathrm{KCl}$ is a salt of strong acid $(\mathrm{HCl})$ and a strong base $[\mathrm{KOH}]$, thus its solution is neutral with $\mathrm{pH}=7$.
Increasing order of $\mathrm{pH}$ is

\begin{array}{ccc}
\mathrm{CuSO}_4 & < \mathrm{KCl} & < \mathrm{NaCN} \\
\text { I } & \text { III } & \text { II }
\end{array}

